7. AI SQL Tutor
Include an AI-assisted learning feature when a free and responsibly configured AI service is available.

The tutor should:
- Explain SQL concepts in simple language.
- Explain error messages.
- Suggest corrections.
- Provide hints without immediately revealing answers.
- Explain multiple ways to solve a problem.
- Generate additional practice questions.
- Explain query execution.
- Help interpret query results.
- Provide interview-style questions.
Free Access Requirement
The AI tutor must not become a paid feature.

Use the following priority:
1. Built-in explanations and hints stored locally.
2. A locally available question-and-answer knowledge base.
3. Optional AI integration using an available free service or a self-hosted model.
4. If an AI service reaches its free usage limit or becomes unavailable, the rest of the app must continue working normally.
Never require users to provide their own paid API key to access core learning.

Do not expose API keys inside the Android application. Any external AI integration must use a secure backend, appropriate rate limits, and a clearly disclosed privacy policy.

