20. Final Development Instruction for Google AI Studio
Build SQLQuest as a complete, functional Android SQL-learning application, not merely a UI prototype.

Prioritise a working Android application with:
- Complete beginner-to-advanced SQL curriculum.
- Interactive lessons.
- A real SQL execution engine.
- Practical datasets.
- Duolingo-inspired gamification.
- Daily streaks.
- XP and rewards.
- Achievements.
- Interview preparation.
- Real-world projects.
- Progress tracking.
- Offline functionality.
Use Kotlin, Jetpack Compose, Room, and SQLite wherever appropriate.

Implement features incrementally and test each feature before proceeding. Populate the application with actual lesson content, questions, SQL queries, expected results, explanations, and datasets rather than placeholder cards.

The central product principle is simple: every learner receives the complete SQL learning experience for free, from their first SELECT statement to advanced data analyst-level SQL. No subscription, no paywall, no premium tier, and no educational feature restrictions.




One important development recommendation
I'd strongly recommend making the SQL playground, lessons, streaks, XP, projects, and progress tracking work entirely on the device. That way, even if a cloud service or AI provider changes its free limits, learners won't lose access to the core app.